# Part of Cloudberry's isolation2_schedule (src/test/isolation2), as the port
# runs it on a coordinator and three segments: the tests of the schedule
# that bear on M3 -- distributed transactions, distributed snapshots, locks
# and the global deadlock detector -- in the schedule's order.
#
#   run   the test runs here, in both passes; cloudberry/ holds a difference
#         reviewed and kept, where one pass has one
#   skip  it needs what the port does not have yet: the rest of the line says
#         what
#
# The schedule's other tests -- append-optimized tables, bitmap indexes,
# resource queues and groups, FTS and mirrors, the rest of the fault
# injector's places in PostgreSQL's own code -- need M4 to M7, and are not
# listed.
skip lockmodes  pg_locks.gp_segment_id, Cloudberry's column of a system view
run  select_dropped_table
run  concurrent_partition_table_operations_should_not_deadlock
skip starve_case  pg_locks.gp_segment_id and mppsessionid, Cloudberry's columns of a system view
skip create_index_deadlock  a lock on pg_index Cloudberry's CREATE INDEX keeps to the end of its transaction, and PostgreSQL 19's lets go of
skip commit_transaction_block_checkpoint  faults inside PostgreSQL's commit, before_xlog_xact_commit_prepared and onephase_transaction_commit
skip prepare_limit  gpconfig and gpstop, the tools of M7, and a standby coordinator
run  gdd/prepare
run  gdd/dist-deadlock-01
run  gdd/dist-deadlock-04
run  gdd/dist-deadlock-05
run  gdd/dist-deadlock-06
run  gdd/dist-deadlock-07
run  gdd/dist-deadlock-102
run  gdd/dist-deadlock-103
run  gdd/dist-deadlock-104
run  gdd/dist-deadlock-106
run  gdd/non-lock-105
skip gdd/dist-deadlock-upsert  INSERT ... ON CONFLICT into a distributed table, which neither planner plans yet
run  gdd/delete-deadlock-root-leaf-concurrent-op
run  gdd/update-deadlock-root-leaf-concurrent-op
run  gdd/local-deadlock-03
run  gdd/end
run  alter_blocks_for_update_and_viceversa
skip reader_waits_for_lock  pg_locks.mppiswriter and gp_session_id, Cloudberry's columns of a system view and its session's id
run  vacuum_recently_dead_tuple_due_to_distributed_snapshot
run  distributedlog-bug
run  distributed_snapshot
run  sharedsnapshot
skip export_distributed_snapshot  the distributed fields of Cloudberry's pg_export_snapshot() file, which the port's has no need of: the coordinator's snapshot is the distributed one
